      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Hi, thanks for the feature request!\n\nRegarding the title:\n\n\"Please include support for blended shapes and simplifed parameters in the new native FT\"\n\nSupport is included (and surpassed) by the Parameter Behaviors and custom expressions feature. What this feature request appears to be is a request for presets for the custom expressions.\n\nThis was actually considered early on and is currently not planned.\n\nA goal of the new FT system is to provide flexibility to achieve what was previously achieved regarding blendshapes in the animator, outside of the animator, allowing perf optimization.\n\nThough we know doing stuff in the animator is sometimes unavoidable, so \"Forward to Animator\" is an option available to people who need it, it's not encouraged.\n\nPre-native FT had to deal with very limited parameter space and so the paradigm around that extending in to the new system by adding presets for custom expressions would somewhat bake in an artifact of this transitionary period.\n\nOverall, we don't want to necessarily encourage people from using animator-only prefabs as is, but also don't want to stop them either. (And of course, the old non-native stuff will still work too)\n\nI would suggest using the \"Copy All\" and \"Paste\" features of the Parameter Expressions to speed up any migration work if that's your concern (I've already seen community examples shared of common conversions into custom expression). The \"Paste\" feature can single-click paste many Parameter Expressions at once, and the clipboard format is plain text, so copied setups can be shared around.\n\nSeparately, regarding the 512 instructions limit, that is a little conservative yeah, I'll look into increasing it.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
