      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{6161a61a2c0de966b4e43486|full_name} It wasn't my intention for them to necessarily be just presets, though I wouldn't be opposed. I was hoping for a more seamless integration, the values are already provided by VRCFT after all. Also they're not necessarily all about parameter space, since which parameters you use and which shapes you use weren't linked. A lot of it is just about practicality, a lot of hardware doesn't even track the individual shapes that make up some of the blended shapes. And of course backwards-compatibility with existing avatars, the closer the new system is to being a drop-in the better, in my opinion. I feel like leaving them out is just encouraging people to rely on third-party scripts to auto-fill all the required Parameter Behaviors. There are worse fates I suppose, just lots more work for me lol. Anyway I will say the Parameter Behaviors / custom expressions system is a godsend, kudos to whoever's idea that was.",
